# Slice 276: two root heads of y; the bare path selects neither.  Before the forms stopped assigning (plan M7, step 4)
# the second head was written `y: 7`, an assignment read as a head; a form with a colon on a known place is refused
# now (colon_known_body_refused), and the second head is the declaration's repeat.
D:
    int: y 3
    int: y 7
end: D
int: code D\y
send: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
